Phase A of the subtraction programme: nothing is deleted, every item is a guard on a destruction path, and they ship a release AHEAD of the deletions they exist to make safe — removals fail CLOSED where additions fail open. A1 SHIPS THE PROJECT-CUSTOM REGION EXTRACTOR AS CODE (`user-level-reference/skills/sync-template/region.sh`) rather than as prose, because two independent consumers implemented "is the region empty?" from the paragraph and both got the REASSURING answer wrongly — `BEGIN\s*-->` matches nothing against a marker carrying trailing prose, and a language-level recursive glob skips dot-directories, i.e. all of `.claude/`; one measured "zero regions" across a repo with eleven, at which point accept-template destroys the region with the disqualifier cleared. A2 makes deletion of a region-bearing file UNREACHABLE rather than defaulted-away-from — a second acknowledgement loses to fatigue, so `TEMPLATE_DELETED × non-empty region` offers only relocate-or-defer, prints the region verbatim, and byte-compares after a relocate, which makes "provably elsewhere" mechanical instead of asserted. A3 rescopes step 2b's backup to what the destructive operation TOUCHES rather than what the manifest KNOWS, because manifest membership tracks template PROVENANCE, not importance: the untracked file in a rewritten directory is the only one nobody can regenerate. A4 keys the reference sweep on the reference SHAPE across five binding forms, two of which fail OPEN and SILENT — a bare name grep is 28:1 noise (195 hits, 7 real) and dies on first use. A5 makes "deliberately exempt" distinguishable from "silently fell out", statically in the gate, because the runtime fix is unavailable: hook stderr was measured not to reach the lead, so a warning nobody receives is the same silence with more code. A6 fixes a merge gate that verified the WRONG HEAD — `artifact.sha == HEAD` is meaningful only on some topologies, and on a controller sitting on trunk the remedy it printed manufactured a green receipt for content already merged. Every guard ships a control and every control was verified BY DELETING ITS GUARD; the region controls run against PLANTED content, because a census of three consumer repos found ZERO real region content and a guard that cannot fail proves nothing.
